What is the output of the following C code snippet?

```c
int a = 10, b = 20, c = 30;
int result = a > b ? a : b > c ? b : c;
printf("%d", result);
```

Consider the following recursive C function:

```c
void print(int n) {
    if (n < 0) return;
    printf("%d ", n);
    print(n - 1);
    printf("%d ", n);
}
```
What is the output when `print(2)` is called?

Consider the following C function:

```c
int f(int n) {
    static int r = 0;
    if (n <= 0) return 1;
    if (n > 3) {
        r = n;
        return f(n-2) + 2;
    }
    return f(n-1) + r;
}
```
What is the value of `f(5)`?

Assuming a 32-bit architecture where `char` is 1 byte, `short` is 2 bytes, and `int` is 4 bytes, what is the `sizeof` the following structure (assuming standard alignment)?

```c
struct Data {
    char a;
    int b;
    short c;
};
```
